{"tool_name":"patternexplorer","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"patternexplorer","home":"http://ncbr.muni.cz/PatternQuery","summary":"A web application to define, extract, and analyze structural patterns or biomolecular complexes in real-time.","addition_date":"2015-12-01T17:38:22Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:50:37.942795Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1.0"],"collections":["CEITEC","Czech Republic","ELIXIR-CZ","LCC NCBR"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:patternexplorer","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"david.sehnal@gmail.com","name":"David Sehnal","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"xpravda@ncbr.muni.cz","name":"Luk\u00e1\u0161 Pravda","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"webchemistryhelp@gmail.com","name":"Primary Contact","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://webchem.ncbr.muni.cz"},{"email":"david.sehnal@gmail.com","name":"David Sehnal","typeRole":["Support"]},{"email":"xpravda@ncbr.muni.cz","name":"Luk\u00e1\u0161 Pravda","typeRole":["Support"]},{"email":"webchemistryhelp@gmail.com","name":"Primary Contact","typeRole":["Support"],"url":"http://webchem.ncbr.muni.cz"},{"name":"ELIXIR-CZ","typeEntity":"Consortium"},{"name":"ELIXIR-CZ","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Masaryk University, Brno, Czech Republic","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["Citation instructions"],"url":"http://nar.oxfordjournals.org/citmgr?gca=nar%3B43%2FW1%2FW383"},{"type":["General"],"url":"http://webchem.ncbr.muni.cz/Wiki/PatternQuery:UserManual"},{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"http://webchem.ncbr.muni.cz/Platform/Home/About"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"},{"term":"Tertiary structure format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2033"},{"term":"mmCIF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1477"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"},{"term":"Protein structural motif recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0245"},{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0883"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"},{"term":"Tertiary structure format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2033"}]}]}],"maturity":"Legacy","name":"PatternQuery","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-CZ","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkv561","metadata":{"abstract":"Well defined biomacromolecular patterns such as binding sites, catalytic sites, specific protein or nucleic acid sequences, etc. precisely modulate many important biological phenomena. We introduce PatternQuery, a web-based application designed for detection and fast extraction of such patterns. The application uses a unique query language with Pythonlike syntax to define the patterns that will be extracted from datasets provided by the user, or from the entire Protein Data Bank (PDB). Moreover, the database-wide search can be restricted using a variety of criteria, such as PDB ID, resolution, and organism of origin, to provide only relevant data. The extraction generally takes a few seconds for several hundreds of entries, up to approximately one hour for the whole PDB. The detected patterns are made available for download to enable further processing, as well as presented in a clear tabular and graphical form directly in the browser. The unique design of the language and the provided service could pave the way towards novel PDB-wide analyses, which were either difficult or unfeasible in the past. The application is available free of charge at http://ncbr.muni.cz/PatternQuery.","autho